    "1)Explain the architecture of Faster R-CNN and its components. Discuss the role of \n",
    "each component in the object detection pipeline? \n",
    "\n",
    "Ans:- \n",
    "\n",
    "Faster R-CNN (Region-based Convolutional Neural Network) is an advanced deep \n",
    "learning model used for object detection. \n",
    "It not only classifies objects in an image but also locates them by drawing bounding \n",
    "boxes around each detected object. \n",
    "It improves the speed and accuracy of earlier models like R-CNN and Fast R-CNN by \n",
    "introducing a special module called the Region Proposal Network (RPN). \n",
    "Architecture of Faster R-CNN \n",
    "The Faster R-CNN architecture mainly consists of the following four key components: \n",
    "1. Convolutional Layers (Feature Extraction) \n",
    "2. Region Proposal Network (RPN) \n",
    "3. ROI Pooling (Region of Interest Pooling) \n",
    "4. Fully Connected Layers (Classification and Bounding Box Regression) \n",
    "1. Convolutional Layers (Feature Extraction): \n",
    "• The input image is first passed through several convolutional and pooling layers \n",
    "(often using a pre-trained CNN such as VGG16, ResNet, or AlexNet). \n",
    "• These layers extract feature maps that contain spatial and semantic information \n",
    "about the image, such as edges, textures, and object shapes. \n",
    "• These feature maps are shared between the RPN and the ROI pooling layer, \n",
    "making the network efficient. \n",
    "Role: \n",
    "Extract meaningful features from the input image that can be used for object detection. \n",
    "2. Region Proposal Network (RPN): \n",
    "• The RPN is the core innovation in Faster R-CNN. \n",
    "• It scans the feature map and proposes candidate regions (anchors) where \n",
    "objects are likely to be located. \n",
    "• Each anchor box is classified as either object or background, and coordinates \n",
    "are refined to generate better region proposals. \n",
    "Role: \n",
    "Generates possible bounding boxes (region proposals) automatically, removing the \n",
    "need for slow external algorithms like Selective Search (used in earlier R-CNN versions). \n",
    "3. ROI Pooling (Region of Interest Pooling): \n",
    "• After region proposals are generated, ROI Pooling extracts fixed-size feature \n",
    "maps from these regions so they can be fed into fully connected layers. \n",
    "• It takes variable-sized proposals and converts them into fixed-size feature \n",
    "vectors (e.g., 7×7). \n",
    "Role: \n",
    "Ensures all proposed regions have the same feature dimensions, allowing consistent \n",
    "processing in later stages. \n",
    "4. Fully Connected Layers (Classification and Bounding Box Regression): \n",
    "• These layers take the pooled feature maps and perform two tasks \n",
    "simultaneously: \n",
    "1. Classification: Predicts the object class (e.g., dog, car, person, etc.). \n",
    "2. Bounding Box Regression: Refines the coordinates of the bounding box \n",
    "to improve localization accuracy. \n",
    "Role: \n",
    "Performs the final decision-making — identifies what the object is and where exactly it \n",
    "is located. \n",
    "Overall Object Detection Pipeline in Faster R-CNN \n",
    "1. The input image is passed through a CNN backbone (e.g., ResNet) to extract \n",
    "features. \n",
    "2. The RPN generates region proposals from the feature map. \n",
    "3. The ROI Pooling layer extracts fixed-size feature maps for each proposal. \n",
    "4. The Fully Connected Layers classify the object and adjust bounding box \n",
    "coordinates. \n",
    "5. The final output is a set of bounding boxes with labels and confidence scores. \n",
    "Advantages of Faster R-CNN \n",
    "• Much faster than earlier R-CNN versions due to the Region Proposal Network. \n",
    "• Achieves high accuracy in both object classification and localization. \n",
    "• End-to-end trainable — both RPN and detection network share features."
   ]
  },
